.TH ZORO-FETCH 1 "2026" "Zoro Linux 10" "Zoro Linux Manual"

.SH NAME
zoro\-fetch \- Zoro Linux system information display tool

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zoro\-fetch
.RI [ options ]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zoro-fetch
is a custom system information tool for Zoro Linux, replacing neofetch/fastfetch.
It displays system information alongside a stylised three-sword ASCII art logo
in the Zoro Linux colour palette (green, gold, silver).

.SH OUTPUT FIELDS
.TP
.B OS
Operating system name and version.
.TP
.B Kernel
Linux kernel version.
.TP
.B Uptime
System uptime in days, hours, minutes.
.TP
.B Packages
Number of installed RPM packages.
.TP
.B Shell
Current shell (bash, zsh, etc.).
.TP
.B Resolution
Display resolution (if graphical session).
.TP
.B DE/WM
Desktop environment: ZoroDeck (GNOME) or ZoroBlade (KDE).
.TP
.B Terminal
Terminal emulator name.
.TP
.B CPU
CPU model and core count.
.TP
.B GPU
GPU model (if detected).
.TP
.B RAM
Used / Total memory.

.SH AUTOMATIC EXECUTION
By default, zoro-fetch runs automatically on interactive shell login via
.IR /etc/profile.d/zoro-fetch.sh .
It only runs if a graphical display or SSH session is detected.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/zoro-fetch
The zoro-fetch binary.
.TP
.I /etc/profile.d/zoro-fetch.sh
Login script that triggers zoro-fetch.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zoro-linux (7),
.BR zoro-harden (8)

.SH AUTHOR
The Zoro Linux Project <devel@zorolinux.org>
